# Manual API requests for the VS Code REST Client extension.
# Start the backend with npm run dev from bookmg-repo-be.
# Match baseUrl to BASE_URL in your backend .env.
# Click Send Request above a request, or use Ctrl+Alt+R with the cursor inside it.
# Replace coverId with a coverId returned by search before requesting a cover.

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:3000
@coverId = 15155833
@workId = OL82563W

### Health — expected 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### General search — expected 200 with data and pagination meta
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/books/search?q=Harry%20Potter&page=1&limit=20

### Next page
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/books/search?q=Harry%20Potter&page=2&limit=20

### Search by title
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/books/search?q=Harry%20Potter&field=title&page=1&limit=20

### Search by author
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/books/search?q=J.%20K.%20Rowling&field=author&page=1&limit=20

### Cover — JPEG if available; 404 COVER_NOT_FOUND if missing
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/books/covers/{{coverId}}

### Discover books about a subject; same normalized response and pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/books/search?q=Magic&field=subject&page=1&limit=20

### Multi-word subject, second page
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/books/search?q=Juvenile%20fiction&field=subject&page=2&limit=20

### Missing keyword — expected 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/books/search?page=1&limit=20

### Invalid pagination — expected 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/books/search?q=Harry%20Potter&page=0

### Inspect raw Open Library work details (manual diagnostic only)
# Replace workId with an id from our search response, e.g. OL82563W.
# Open Library search calls this field key, sometimes /works/OL82563W.
# The frontend must use backend endpoints; this direct call is only for inspection.
GET https://openlibrary.org/works/{{workId}}.json
Accept: application/json
User-Agent: MiniReadingTracker/1.0

### Normalized book details through the backend; expected 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/books/{{workId}}

### Inspect raw Read API (diagnostic only; availability is not guaranteed)
GET https://openlibrary.org/api/volumes/brief/olid/OL23747519M.json

### Detail includes readingUrl (HTTPS link or null); does not write to the database
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/books/OL15328717W
